<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1, mechanism 4a — the walking hearth's actual effect.

       Applied and re-stamped every 60 ticks by CompFurnaceWarmthAura to every
       pawn within a few cells of a furnace-beast. HediffComp_Disappears does
       the expiry: 180 ticks, re-set on each refresh, so leaving the herd loses
       the warmth within about three seconds of game time and nothing has to
       track who walked away.

       TWO OFFSETS, BOTH RULED. the_pyrelands.md §5, verbatim: furnace-beasts
       "are welcome company in the cold and terrible company in the dry". So:

         ComfyTemperatureMin -14   you tolerate 14 degC more cold. This is the
                                   "travelers follow the herds for warmth"
                                   line (§4) made mechanical. Calibration: the
                                   biggest comparable vanilla hediff offset is
                                   Inhumanized at -16; a beast you are standing
                                   next to should be worth a little less than
                                   a permanent psychic transformation.
         ComfyTemperatureMax  -6   and you tolerate 6 degC LESS heat. Standing
                                   beside a stove on a 55 degC dayside map is
                                   a mistake, and the sheet says so.

       Hediff stat offsets are real: StatWorker.cs:508 reads every hediff's
       CurStage.statOffsets into the pawn's stat value.

       isBad false (mixed effect, not purely bad — it helps in the cold as
       much as it hurts in the heat) but still a visible label: the player
       must be able to SEE why a colonist who walked past the herd is
       suddenly sweating.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RM_FurnaceWarmth</defName>
    <label>furnace-warmed</label>
    <description>Standing close enough to a furnace-beast to feel the heat coming off its hide. It is a considerable comfort in the cold and an active liability in the sun.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <ComfyTemperatureMin>-14</ComfyTemperatureMin>
          <ComfyTemperatureMax>-6</ComfyTemperatureMax>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Disappears">
        <disappearsAfterTicks>180</disappearsAfterTicks>
        <showRemainingTime>false</showRemainingTime>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_DEDICATED_GRAZER_1 — the burrow state itself.
       Applied by RM_JobDriver_Burrow for as long as an extension-carrying
       pawn is sheltering from a nearby fire front; removed by the same
       driver's AddFinishAction on every exit path (safe emergence, the
       safety-cap timeout, or the job being interrupted).

       TWO STAT OFFSETS, same idiom RM_FurnaceBeast's permanent statBases
       use for total fire immunity (ArmorRating_Heat, Flammability), applied
       here only WHILE burrowed rather than always:
         ArmorRating_Heat +4.0   comfortably past the point the vanilla armor
                                  formula treats as near-total mitigation —
                                  "the fire pass[es] over" it (the_pyrelands.md
                                  §4), not merely resists it. [INVENTED]
         Flammability     -1.0   zeroes the default 1.0 base outright, so a
                                  burrowed pawn standing in a burning cell
                                  cannot itself catch alight.

       isBad false: this is the mechanism working as intended, not an
       affliction — the player should read it as "sheltering", not "hurt".
  ======================================================================== -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RM_Burrowed</defName>
    <label>burrowed</label>
    <description>Gone to ground, sheltering from a fire front passing overhead. Nearly immune to heat and flame while it holds; the animal cannot do anything else until it surfaces.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <ArmorRating_Heat>4.0</ArmorRating_Heat>
          <Flammability>-1.0</Flammability>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
